==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*komterād}}, ablative singular feminine of {{m|itc-pro|*komteros||the other of the two who meet, opposite}}. The ablative singular masculine/neuter of the same is continued in {{cog|la|contrō-}}, cognate to {{cog|osc|contrud}}. Ultimately from {{inh|la|ine-pro||*ḱómteros}}, from {{com|ine-pro|*ḱóm|t1=next to, at, with, along|*-teros|pos2=contrastive suffix|nocat=1}}; thus, a {{dbt|la|cum|nocap=1}}, comparable to the relation between {{m|la|intrā}} and {{m|la|in}}, and  {{m|la|extrā}} and {{m|la|ex}}, but unlike these lacking external cognates, and therefore of Italic origin.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|contrā|132}}</ref>

The change from instrumental/ablative to accusative is caused by {{m|ine-pro|*-teros}} used adverbially.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|contrā}}

